{"pages":[{"w":612.0,"h":792.0,"s":[[13.889,2.206,18.17,3.8,3.431,"EQUINOX"],[13.889,5.306,14.953,1.205,1.078,"Q U A N T I T A T I V E"],[69.444,2.807,15.359,1.643,1.471,"India Equity Research"],[69.444,4.27,11.266,1.46,1.307,"16 November 2026"],[13.889,10.995,15.512,3.651,3.268,"ABB India"],[13.889,14.731,31.546,2.373,2.124,"Orders strong, multiple breathless"],[13.889,20.845,52.931,1.809,1.634,"ABB India shares are up 46% over 12m and 39% YTD, sitting just below the"],[13.889,22.289,52.931,1.809,1.634,"₹7,925 traded high. Q3 CY26 (Jul-Sep) revenue grew 19% to ₹3,738 cr, Op"],[13.889,23.733,52.931,1.809,1.634,"EBITA rose 15% to ₹484 cr and continuing PAT rose 10% to ₹440 cr. Reported"],[13.889,25.177,52.931,1.809,1.634,"profit, including discontinued robotics operations, was ₹443 cr. Results were"],[13.889,26.621,52.931,1.809,1.634,"announced on Friday after the close, so the 13-Nov price has not yet absorbed"],[13.889,28.065,52.959,1.809,1.634,"them. At ₹7,054, ABB trades at 89x CY26E continuing EPS and 52x CY28E"],[13.889,29.509,3.196,1.809,1.634,"EPS."],[13.889,31.995,52.951,1.809,1.634,"1) Demand is extraordinary: record 9M CY26 orders of ₹13,376 cr (+43% y/y),"],[13.889,33.439,52.951,1.809,1.634,"including ₹4,733 cr in Q3 (+56%, a quarterly record) — data centres, utilities,"],[13.889,34.883,52.934,1.809,1.634,"metals and mining, food & beverage, cement and buildings and infrastructure. 2)"],[13.889,36.328,52.931,1.809,1.634,"Mix matters: Electrification delivered record orders of ₹2,780 cr (+117%) and"],[13.889,37.772,52.931,1.809,1.634,"revenue of ₹1,927 cr (+40%); Motion orders ₹1,477 cr (+15%), revenue ₹1,336"],[13.889,39.216,52.931,1.809,1.634,"cr (+14%); Automation orders ₹499 cr (+4%), revenue ₹505 cr (-16%). 3) The"],[13.889,40.684,52.934,1.809,1.634,"swing factor is profitability: 9M EBITDA margin was 13.5% (vs 15.9% a year"],[13.889,42.128,52.931,1.809,1.634,"ago) and Q3 margin 14.8%; per management, pressures were commodity and"],[13.889,43.572,52.964,1.809,1.634,"logistics costs, currency volatility, pricing pressure and lower volumes, not one-"],[13.889,45.016,52.737,1.809,1.634,"offs. Price hikes can improve margins, but the market already expects execution."],[13.889,47.502,52.934,1.809,1.634,"Our target is the average of two explicit legs: 60.0x CY28E EQe EPS (₹8,183)"],[13.889,48.946,52.931,1.809,1.634,"and the published mean (₹7,035), producing ₹7,610 (+7.9%; Neutral). The"],[13.889,50.39,52.992,1.809,1.634,"forward assumptions are aligned to Motilal Oswal's 14-Nov CY26–28 recovery"],[13.889,51.834,52.934,1.809,1.634,"outlook; the target and rating are Equinox's. ABB deserves scarcity economics"],[13.889,53.278,52.957,1.809,1.634,"— 75%-owned by ABB Ltd, ₹12,927 cr backlog, capex announcement of USD"],[13.889,54.722,52.951,1.809,1.634,"75m and secular electrification/data-centre demand. Motilal is Buy (₹8,200),"],[13.889,56.167,52.951,1.809,1.634,"while Yahoo shows 7 Buy, 8 Hold and 12 Sell/Strong Sell. This is not a short —"],[13.889,57.611,52.992,1.809,1.634,"visibility is real. It is also not a free lunch at 89x CY26E EPS; margin recovery"],[13.889,59.055,28.656,1.809,1.634,"must show up, not merely remain promised."],[13.889,61.542,13.042,1.643,1.471,"Price Performance"],[14.451,70.154,2.306,1.022,0.915,"4,000"],[14.451,66.618,2.306,1.022,0.915,"6,000"],[14.451,63.083,2.306,1.022,0.915,"8,000"],[18.306,70.848,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Jan 26"],[22.929,70.848,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Apr 26"],[27.701,70.848,2.47,1.022,0.915,"Jul 26"],[32.473,70.848,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Oct 26"],[19.066,72.043,2.387,1.275,1.111,"ABB ("],[21.456,72.069,0.618,1.241,1.111,"₹"],[22.069,72.043,0.303,1.275,1.111,")"],[25.153,72.043,7.901,1.275,1.111,"NIFTY 50 (rebased)"],[20.051,73.179,1.972,1.387,1.209,"YTD"],[25.13,73.179,1.433,1.387,1.209,"1m"],[30.516,73.179,1.433,1.387,1.209,"3m"],[34.446,73.179,1.984,1.387,1.209,"12m"],[15.277,74.244,1.691,1.387,1.209,"Abs"],[19.132,74.244,2.811,1.387,1.209,"38.6%"],[24.211,74.244,2.26,1.387,1.209,"1